<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>SpectraEngine.Editing.Tests</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\SpectraEngine.Editing\SpectraEngine.Editing.csproj" />
    <!--
      The demo host is referenced for one pure type: DemoStartupOptions, the
      parser that decides whether the synthetic editing self-test runs. That
      switch is an editing concern (it drives the gizmo chain) and its default
      is load-bearing — a self-test left on moves brushes in front of whoever is
      using the editor — so it is pinned here rather than left to a comment.
      Nothing else in the executable is touched, and the dependency runs the
      same direction the solution already does (host -> editing).
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\SpectraEngine.Executable\SpectraEngine.Executable.csproj" />

    <!--
      The GPU-free renderer the Bsp suite already owns, linked rather than
      copied - the same arrangement the Kitchen and Physics suites use. The
      editing suite's own StubRenderer and CompilingRenderer deliberately throw
      on textures, which is right for a gizmo test and makes an AssetManager
      impossible to attach: AttachRenderer creates the magenta placeholder.
      Dropping a MODEL into the viewport needs one, so this suite needs a
      renderer that answers both halves rather than a third partial fake.
    -->
    <Compile Include="..\SpectraEngine.Bsp.Tests\FakeRenderer.cs" Link="FakeRenderer.cs" />
    <Compile Include="..\SpectraEngine.Bsp.Tests\SpatialTestHelpers.cs" Link="SpatialTestHelpers.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
